Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: hardware source colour-key and mirror blits for DirectDraw

DirectDraw advertises only the blits its HAL reports. The D3D9 UMD reported
no colour-key caps and no mirror FX caps, and D3D9Blt rejected SrcColorKey,
MirrorLeftRight and MirrorUpDown, so DirectDraw emulated every colour-key
and mirror blit on the CPU: it read the destination back with a Lock,
blended on the CPU and wrote it back (correct since 0013, but about 9 ms for
one 128x128 colour-key blit on an RTX 5090 host).

D3D9Blt now draws them as one quad (D3D9KeyBlitPipe). The fragment shader
maps each destination pixel to the source texel DirectDraw's emulation
layer picks: floor((k + 0.5) * src / dst) without a mirror, and with any
mirror floor(k * src / dst) on both axes, k counted from the far edge on a
mirrored axis. With SrcColorKey it discards texels whose colour equals the
key, unpacked from the source format, within half a step; alpha never
keys, as in the emulation layer. A surface blitted onto itself is sampled
from a copy of the source rectangle. The quad's vertices go through the
stream uploader: Yttrium reads vertex data after the draw call returns, so
a user vertex buffer on the stack drew garbage in 32-bit processes.

GetCaps(DDRAW) now reports DDRAW_CAPS_COLORKEY, DDRAW_CKEYCAPS_SRCBLT and
DDRAW_FXCAPS_BLTMIRRORLEFTRIGHT | BLTMIRRORUPDOWN. Destination colour keys,
rotation and LinearToSrgb are still rejected and stay emulated.

Evidence: docs/ddraw.md, docs/evidence/ddraw/ (src/ddblit.c compares every
case on X8R8G8B8, R5G6B5 and A8R8G8B8 pixel for pixel against the
emulation layer, x64 and x86).
Origin: vmlab-win3d ddraw worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp
index 5d9257d..76ee0eb 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Adapter.cpp
@@ -737,14 +737,20 @@ D3D9GetCaps(HANDLE hAdapter, const D3DDDIARG_GETCAPS *data)
       if (FAILED(D3D9ValidateData(data, sizeof(DDRAW_CAPS))))
          return E_INVALIDARG;
       memset(data->pData, 0, data->DataSize);
+      /* Source colour-key and mirror blits are drawn by D3D9KeyBlitPipe. */
       ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->Caps = DDRAW_CAPS_ZBLTS |
+                                          DDRAW_CAPS_COLORKEY |
                                           DDRAW_CAPS_BLTDEPTHFILL;
       ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->Caps2 = DDRAW_CAPS2_DYNAMICTEXTURES;
-      ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->CKeyCaps = 0;
-      ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->FxCaps = 0;
-      D3D9Tracef("GetCaps DDRAW caps=0x%08x caps2=0x%08x\n",
+      ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->CKeyCaps = DDRAW_CKEYCAPS_SRCBLT;
+      ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->FxCaps = DDRAW_FXCAPS_BLTMIRRORLEFTRIGHT |
+                                            DDRAW_FXCAPS_BLTMIRRORUPDOWN;
+      D3D9Tracef("GetCaps DDRAW caps=0x%08x caps2=0x%08x ckey=0x%08x "
+                 "fx=0x%08x\n",
                  ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->Caps,
-                 ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->Caps2);
+                 ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->Caps2,
+                 ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->CKeyCaps,
+                 ((DDRAW_CAPS *)data->pData)->FxCaps);
       return S_OK;
    case D3DDDICAPS_DDRAW_MODE_SPECIFIC:
       if (FAILED(D3D9ValidateData(data, sizeof(DDRAW_MODE_SPECIFIC_CAPS))))
